1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Qxd7 5. O-O (5. c4 {To set up a
Maroczy Bind formation}) 5... Nc6 $6 (5... Nf6 {may be best - White then tries
6 e5}) 6. c3 Nf6 7. d4 $1 {This pawn sacrifice is the only way of troubling
Black} (7. Re1 e6 8. d4 cxd4 9. cxd4 d5 10. e5 Ne4 11. Nbd2 Nxd2 12. Bxd2 {
gave White no prospects in Basman-Benko, Hastings 1973-4}) 7... Nxe4 (7... cxd4
8. cxd4 d5 9. e5 Ne4 10. Ne1 $1 {/\ f3}) 8. d5 Ne5 $1 (8... Nb8 $2 9. Re1 Nf6
10. Bg5 $1 Na6 11. c4 Nc7 12. Nc3 e6 13. dxe6 fxe6 14. Nd5 Ncxd5 15. cxd5 e5
16. Rxe5+ $5 {Ivkov-Mecking - Only sturdy souls defend such positions for Black
}) 9. Nxe5 dxe5 10. Re1 Nf6 $6 (10... Nd6 $142 {Diesen-Stean, Hastings 1974})
11. Rxe5 h6 $2 {(An unnecessary finesse)} (11... e6 12. c4 O-O-O $1 {is more
critical}) 12. c4 e6 13. Qe1 $2 (13. Nc3 $142 Bd6 14. dxe6 Qc7 $4 15. Nb5 $1)
13... Bd6 14. Re2 $8 (14. dxe6 Qc7 $1 15. exf7+ Kxf7 $17) 14... O-O 15. dxe6
fxe6 16. Nc3 {On general considerations White should never remove Black's eP
which hinders rather than helps the deployment of pieces} (16. Rxe6 $2 Ng4 $19)
16... Qf7 {Beginning a clever manoeuvre to weaken White's K-side} 17. h3 (17.
Be3 $2 Bxh2+ 18. Kxh2 Ng4+ $1 (18... Qh5+ $2 19. Kg3 $1 g5 20. Qh1 $1) 19. Kg1
(19. Kg3 Qg6 $1 20. Qb1 Rf5) 19... Qh5 20. f3 Qh2+ 21. Kf1 Qh1+ 22. Bg1 Nh2+
23. Kf2 Rxf3+ $1 24. gxf3 Qxf3#) 17... Rae8 18. Be3 Bb8 19. Rd1 Qc7 20. g3 {
Not a pleasant decision. Black's excellent next move prevents Bf4 and prepares
the occupation of f3} Nh5 $1 21. Red2 Rf3 {(/\ Nxg3)} 22. Ne4 $1 b6 23. Nd6 Re7
$6 (23... Ref8 $5 24. Bxh6 $5 gxh6 25. Qxe6+ Kh8 (25... Kh7 $2 26. Nf5 $1 $18)
26. Qxh6+ Qh7 $15) 24. Qe2 Qc6 25. Nc8 $1 Ref7 (25... Re8 26. Rd8 Kf8 27. R1d5
$1 $16) 26. Rd8+ Kh7 27. Qc2+ g6 28. Rg8 $1 R3f5 $1 (28... Kxg8 $2 29. Qxg6+
Ng7 30. Rd8+ Rf8 31. Ne7+ Kh8 32. Qxh6#) (28... e5 $2 29. Rd6 $1 $18) (28...
Rg7 29. Ne7 $18) 29. Ne7 $6 (29. Rdd8 Be5 30. g4 Ng3 $1 $19) 29... Rxe7 30.
Rxb8 Nxg3 $1 31. fxg3 Qc7 32. Bf4 $1 e5 $5 (32... Rxf4 33. Rdd8 $10) 33. Rdd8
exf4 34. Rh8+ Kg7 35. Rbg8+ Kf6 $2 (35... Kf7 $10) 36. Rxh6 Rg7 (36... Re1+ 37.
Kf2 fxg3+ 38. Kxe1 Qe5+ 39. Qe2 $18) 37. Rf8+ $1 Rf7 (37... Ke7 38. Rxf5 gxf5
39. Qe2+ Kf8 (39... Kd8 40. Rh8+ Kd7 41. Qe8+ Kd6 42. Rh6+ $18) 40. Qe6 $1
Rxg3+ 41. Kf2 $18) 38. Rh7 $1 Ke5 (38... Ke7 39. Rfxf7+ Rxf7 40. Qxg6 $18) 39.
Qe2+ Kd4 (39... Kd6 40. Qd2+ Ke5 41. Rfxf7 Rxf7 42. Qxf4+ $1 $18) 40. Re8 {
A rather puzzling game. If there is a forced win for White after 28 Rg8! I
have yet to find it} 1-0

